    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1: Readiness of the Disaster Management Team members and the National Disaster Centre to prepare and respond 
                to disasters enhanced
1). Disaster Management Team annual terms of reference, work plan and were renewed and accountability compact were 
    adopted in Jan 2020; action items were monitored and resolved
2). 50 situation updates
3). 1 humanitarian response plan for COVID-19 
4). 1 updated contingency plan for a La Ni&#xf1;a event
5). 4 Disaster Management Team contingency plans (sudden onset, slow onset, civil unrest, refugee emergency) were 
     created in 2019; sudden-onset and slow-onset were updated in 2020.
6). 5 Provincial Disaster Coordinators received needs assessment training in 2019, but no provincial trainings were carried 
     out.
7).  No formal engagement of civil-military coordination with the Disaster Management  Team.
8). Disaster Management Team members adopted annual terms of reference and member compact that includes specific 
     accountability to uphold the centrality of protection, address gender-based violence, and advocate for protection from 
     sexual exploitation and abuse.
9). Protection Cluster strengthened by a dedicated cluster coordinator, regular meetings of cluster/sub-clusters, active 
     participation in response and contingency planning.
10). Attention elevated on protection concerns under COVID-19 measures.
11), Protection was a focus of revised multi-sectoral response plan for COVID-19

Output 2: Updating the National Disaster Management
1, The Disaster Management Act has not been substantively updated since it was enacted in 1984.</narrative>
     </comment>
