     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1: Readiness of the Disaster Management Team members and the National Disaster Centre to prepare and respond 
    to disasters enhanced
1). Disaster Management Team annual terms of reference, work plan and compact on accountability are renewed and action 
 are monitored
2). Monitor humanitarian situation and coordinate international humanitarian response, needs assessment, and 
  humanitarian financing
3). Disaster Management Team contingency plans and 4W are current, reflecting preparedness to respond to emergencies
4). At least one PDC&#x2019;s preparedness to respond to disasters and emergencies is improved
5). Papua New Guinea participates in Regional Consultative Group for Civil-Military Coordination
6). Gender mainstreaming is improved across project outputs

Output 2: Updating the National Disaster Management
1). Technical inputs to Disaster Management Act have been incorporated.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1: Readiness of the Disaster Management Team members and the National Disaster Centre to prepare and respond 
        to disasters enhanced

1. Disaster Management Team (DMT)
  &#x2022; The DMT renewed its annual terms of reference and accountability compact, approved an annual work plan, and 
    monitored and resolved 3 action items.
  &#x2022; The DMT convened 10 regular meetings, 2 ad hoc meetings, and 1 donor meeting. The DMT Secretariat also met with 
    NGO Development Council and regularly briefed United Nations Country Team and Security Management Team.
  &#x2022; The project monitored and reported on 31 emergencies in addition to fortnightly updates on COVID19 and regular 
    monitoring of African Swine Fever, Fall Army Worm, and movement of asylum seekers from West Papua.

2. Humanitarian monitoring, response coordination
  &#x2022; The project tracked and regularly updated dashboard on international contributions to the COVID-19 response and 
   vaccination rollout.
  &#x2022; Coordinated needs assessments and humanitarian financing for king tide flooding across 
   the country.
